"\n"
"This module allows to set employee quantity for partners, and categorize\n"
"them by ranges.\n"
"\n"
"**Table of contents**\n"
"\n"
".. contents::\n"
"   :local:\n"
"\n"
"Configuration\n"
"=============\n"
"\n"
"To manage available ranges, you need to:\n"
"\n"
"1. Go to *Contacts > Configuration > Ranges by quantity of employees*.\n"
"2. Add or edit any range naming it.\n"
"\n"
"Usage\n"
"=====\n"
"\n"
"To record how many employees a company has:\n"
"\n"
"1. Go to *Contacts* and open a company.\n"
"\n"
"   In Odoo 20.0 a contact is considered a company when it has a *Tax ID*\n"
"   and is not a contact of another company. Individuals and the contacts\n"
"   of a company do not show the employee fields.\n"
"\n"
"2. Open the *Notes* tab. In the *Employee quantity* section, fill in:\n"
"\n"
"   - *Employee Quantity*: the number of employees.\n"
"   - *Employee quantity range*: the range this company belongs to (for\n"
"     example *11-50 Employees*). Ranges are defined in *Contacts >\n"
"     Configuration > Ranges by quantity of employees*.\n"
"\n"
"To see your companies by size:\n"
"\n"
"1. Go to *Contacts* and open the list view.\n"
"2. In the search box, open the filter menu and choose *Group By >\n"
"   Employee Quantity*.\n"
"\n"
"Known issues / Roadmap\n"
"======================\n"
"\n"
"- Put in employee ranges numbers for low and upper limit for having a\n"
"  numerical reference.\n"
"- Don't allow to overlap ranges.\n"
"\n"
